<title>BELGIUM: El Al gains traffic rights for Liege.</title>
<headline>El Al gains traffic rights for Liege.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-01-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Israeli carrier El Al has gained traffic rights to serve Belgium's Liege airport, an airport spokesman told Reuters.</p>
<p>&quot;We have been in contact with El Al's cargo managers very recently but are waiting for some more technical details,&quot; he added.</p>
<p>Currently, the airport does not know when the airline will begin operations to the Belgium airport, he said.</p>
<p>It appears likely that the carrier will use Liege as a stopover on a U.S.-Israel route, sources said.</p>
<p>--Helen Hill, Air Cargo Newsroom Tel +44 171 542 8982 Fax+44 171 542 5017</p>
